    {
      "id": "claim_7accdac862314baa82e1a7422d255887",
      "statement": "tests/sender-bitrate-clock.test.mjs (PR #121) is a regression-guard file that `npm test` runs via `node --no-warnings --test \\\"tests/*.test.mjs\\\"` (bringing the repo's regression-guard file count from 44 to 45 at that time; the repo now carries 55 regression-guard files). It pins the sender bitrate accept-time clock reset: onSend's closure fileStats started with startTime at the Send click, so any waiting-accept delay inflated the 'Sending: X/sec' denominator; the EVENT_RECEIVER_ACCEPT handler now writes fileStats.startTime = Date.now() making the denominator time-since-ACCEPT, mirroring the receiver's onAccept entry clock. After the per-file progress + bitrate UI-update block was deduplicated into the shared src/utils/transferProgress.ts helper (updateTransferProgress, PR #136), the test keeps pinning the clock the denominator derives from — the accept-time clock, reset exactly once in the EVENT_RECEIVER_ACCEPT handler before the pipeline starts — and verifies the helper's shape against it; the zero-elapsed floor the denominator is wrapped in is pinned separately by tests/bitrate-zero-elapsed-guard.test.mjs.",
